    ["它来自\"秘偶大师\"罗萨戈的遗物。那个死去的人曾用它约束过多少秘密？\n莎伦苍白的手指抚过橘黄的纸面。把它递给了克莱恩，在煤气灯坏掉的僻静街道上，让明亮的光芒见证一个新的誓言。\n符号次第亮起，暖流一闪而逝。\n\"我好了。\"克莱恩将公证书递还了回去。\n莎伦平静颔首，淡漠的身影消失在车厢内。\n而那张空白的纸页，会继续等待一个新的约定——那是太阳永不熄灭的见证。"] = "It came from the relics of the \"Marionettist\" Rosago. How many secrets had that dead man constrained with it? \n Sharron's pale fingers brushed over the orange paper surface. She handed it to Klein, and in the quiet street where the gas lamp was broken, let the bright light witness a new vow. \n The symbols lit up one by one, and a warm current flashed and vanished. \n \"I'm done,\" Klein handed the notarization document back. \n Sharron nodded calmly, and her indifferent figure disappeared into the carriage. \n And that blank page would continue to wait for a new agreement—that is the witness of the sun that never goes out.",
